  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-JOR105</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved existing programmes to extend social security coverage through the progressive establishment of a national SPF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme supports Jordan in advancing a more sustainable, inclusive, and well-integrated social protection system that balances adequacy, affordability, and expanded coverage. It strengthens national capacity to implement reforms under the National Social Protection Strategy 2025&#x2013;2033 by improving policy design, governance, and coordination, and enhancing the financial and administrative performance of social insurance schemes. During the biennium, it focuses on extending coverage to underserved groups&#x2014;including informal, self-employed, and non-standard workers, as well as women and older persons&#x2014;through more inclusive and affordable schemes, contribution support measures, and exploration of social allowances. It also promotes stronger linkages between social protection and labour market policies to support pathways to formalisation and provide effective protection during economic transitions. The programme benefits government institutions, workers, and employers, particularly those in vulnerable employment situations, and is implemented through a coordinated approach involving national stakeholders and development partners to ensure sustainability and alignment with national priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
